# REST API requests for the Visual Studio / VS Code REST Client.
# Start the app (dotnet run), then run "Login" first and paste the token into @token below.

@host = https://localhost:7180

### 1. Login (Sales Executive demo account)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "sales1@acxiomcrm.local", "password": "Sales@12345" }

### 2. Paste the token from step 1 here
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### List customers (200, scoped to the caller)
GET {{host}}/api/customers?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Same call without a token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/customers

### Create customer (201). Run twice to see 409 (duplicate email/phone)
POST {{host}}/api/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Demo Customer", "email": "demo.customer@example.com", "phone": "9811122233", "companyName": "Demo Pvt Ltd" }

### Invalid payload -> 400 with field errors
POST {{host}}/api/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "", "email": "bad", "phone": "123" }

### Get / update / delete customer 1
GET {{host}}/api/customers/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
PUT {{host}}/api/customers/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Anita Rao", "email": "anita.rao@example.com", "phone": "9876500001", "status": "Active" }

### Leads
GET {{host}}/api/leads
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/leads
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "leadName": "API Lead", "email": "api.lead@example.com", "phone": "9822233344", "source": "Website", "status": "New", "priority": "High", "expectedValue": 150000 }

### Opportunities - Amount 0 -> 400 "Opportunity Amount must be greater than 0."
POST {{host}}/api/opportunities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "opportunityName": "Bad deal", "customerId": 1, "amount": 0, "stage": "Proposal", "probability": 40, "expectedCloseDate": "2030-01-01" }

### Opportunities - valid
POST {{host}}/api/opportunities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "opportunityName": "API deal", "customerId": 1, "amount": 250000, "stage": "Proposal", "probability": 40, "expectedCloseDate": "2030-01-01" }

### Probability 101 -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/opportunities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "opportunityName": "Bad prob", "customerId": 1, "amount": 100, "stage": "Proposal", "probability": 101, "expectedCloseDate": "2030-01-01" }

### Follow-ups - date in the past -> 400 "Follow-up date cannot be earlier than today."
POST {{host}}/api/followups
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subject": "Old", "customerId": 1, "followUpDate": "2020-01-01", "followUpType": "Call", "status": "Planned" }

### Pipeline report (scoped)
GET {{host}}/api/reports/pipeline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Logout (all tokens issued before now stop working)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
